fact WorkItem(id: "WI-209", description: some(value: "Parametric effect substitution at call sites. When a called operation O declares effects like Modify[c] where c is one of O's parameters, the effect emitted at the call site O(arg0, ...) should be Modify[arg0_name] (substitute c → the actual arg's referent name). Today's typer treats Modify[c] as a literal effect, so when a body calls Cell.set(s, ...) inside an op declaring effects Modify[s], the typer sees Modify[c] (from Cell.set) vs declared Modify[s] (in calling op) and reports 'undeclared effect: Modify[T = c]'. The mechanism: in kb/typing.rs check_apply (line 593), after the existing unify_types loop builds subst from arg-type unification, also walk each of op.effects through a param-to-arg name substitution map (extracted from each var_ref arg's symbol) and through the existing subst. Replace Term::Ref(spec_param_sym) with Term::Ref(arg_var_sym) wherever it appears nested in the effect. Today walk_type is applied only to op.return_type; effects pass through unchanged. Acceptance: cargo-test green; the FileBasedWorkitemStore.commit and .next_id bodies in anthill-todo/store.anthill type-check cleanly with effects {Modify[s], Error} on commit and Modify[s] on next_id (no 'undeclared effect: Modify[T = c]' / 'Modify[T = store]'). Out of scope: (i) polymorphic type-arg propagation through nested polymorphic ops like Stream.head — separate WI; (ii) Modify-transitivity (Modify[s] covers Modify[s.field]) per proposal 037 — separate WI; (iii) signature inheritance from spec via fact (the original WI-209 framing as 'inheritance'); (iv) call-site dispatch (problem B, now WI-210). Independent of WI-188 (entity copy) and WI-189 (reflect operators). Driver: WI-203 phase-2 bodies + bundle phase 3."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-203"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-09T21:39:00Z"))
